; Innermost wins (MAC-HYG-9 M3): a `syntax/for` binding pushed
; inside a template binder of the same spelling answers where the
; template did. Here the template `let` binds `g` to 41 and an
; argument-position `syntax/for` in its body iterates `g` over the
; struct's fields; each for-body `g` resolves to the iteration -
; the inner binder - so the field names `x` and `y` arrive where
; no variable is bound, and the checker refuses both as AX3001.
; The opposite precedence, template binder first, would answer the
; `let`'s 41; it was the expander's rule before M3, when this program
; answered 41 as a selfhost case. Scope resolution takes the inner
; binder whatever its kind, so a field name arriving unbound is the
; checker's true AX3001, pinned by this fixture's golden. The rule is
; MAC-HYG-9's M3 step in docs/macro-system.md, and M4 left it as the
; only resolution the expander has.
(struct Point
  (x : Int)
  (y : Int))

(macro (probe S) (let ((g 41))
  (S (syntax/for (g (syntax/fields S)) g))))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((p (probe Point)))
    p.x))
